1
00:00:00,659 --> 00:00:01,689
Hi, everybody.

2
00:00:01,689 --> 00:00:02,690
I'm Lynn.

3
00:00:02,690 --> 00:00:04,609
Thanks for watching my video.

4
00:00:04,609 --> 00:00:07,772
Today we're gonna talk about not worrying

5
00:00:07,772 --> 00:00:10,754
about making mistakes in English.

6
00:00:10,754 --> 00:00:14,040
When you speak English, you might make a mistake.

7
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:15,680
That's okay.

8
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:19,140
This is a really helpful video, so keep watching.

9
00:00:22,510 --> 00:00:26,141
A lot of my students are scared to speak English

10
00:00:26,141 --> 00:00:29,458
because they're afraid of making a mistake.

11
00:00:29,458 --> 00:00:32,408
They think their English needs to be perfect

12
00:00:32,408 --> 00:00:34,461
before they even try.

13
00:00:34,461 --> 00:00:37,645
Well, I'm here to tell you that's not true.

14
00:00:37,645 --> 00:00:39,728
Everyone makes mistakes.

15
00:00:39,728 --> 00:00:42,210
It's part of the learning process.

16
00:00:42,210 --> 00:00:45,921
So my tip for you is just try speaking

17
00:00:45,921 --> 00:00:48,976
even if your English has a lot of mistakes,

18
00:00:48,976 --> 00:00:53,400
or you think it sounds broken, that's okay.

19
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:56,148
Speaking in English is much better

20
00:00:56,148 --> 00:00:58,543
than not speaking at all.

21
00:00:58,543 --> 00:01:01,061
If you don't try to use your English,

22
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:03,205
then you'll never improve.

23
00:01:03,205 --> 00:01:06,215
It's much more important and useful

24
00:01:06,215 --> 00:01:08,828
to speak English even with some mistakes

25
00:01:08,828 --> 00:01:11,197
than to not speak at all.

26
00:01:11,197 --> 00:01:14,373
Everyone makes mistakes when learning English.

27
00:01:14,373 --> 00:01:16,827
And the person that you're talking to

28
00:01:16,827 --> 00:01:18,440
can tell you your mistakes.

29
00:01:18,450 --> 00:01:21,143
And that helps you to learn and improve.

30
00:01:21,143 --> 00:01:22,916
So the best thing you can do

31
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:25,017
is just try speaking

32
00:01:25,017 --> 00:01:27,520
even if you have a lot of mistakes,

33
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:29,420
that's okay.

34
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:31,048
Okay, students.

35
00:01:31,048 --> 00:01:35,048
So speak, speak, and speak some more.

36
00:01:35,048 --> 00:01:36,889
Just keep trying.

37
00:01:36,889 --> 00:01:39,521
I know when my students speak English

38
00:01:39,521 --> 00:01:42,339
and they make a mistake, I don't care.

39
00:01:42,339 --> 00:01:45,949
In fact, I'm really happy that they're trying their English.

40
00:01:45,949 --> 00:01:48,068
I know English is hard,

41
00:01:48,068 --> 00:01:49,420
but I believe in you guys.

42
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:51,455
And I know you can do it.

43
00:01:51,455 --> 00:01:52,992
Thanks for watching everybody

44
00:01:52,992 --> 00:01:54,470
and see you next time.

